.TH NOXMEM 1 "September 2026" "noxmem 0.0.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
NoxMem \- a terminal UI for live GoLang heap memory profiling.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noxmem
[\fB-t\fR|\fB--target\fR \fISTRINGS\fR]
[\fB-r\fR|\fB--rate\fR \fIREFRESH_RATE\fR]
[\fB-h\fR|\fB--help\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NoxMem
A terminal UI for live Go heap profiling. Connect it to your application's pprof endpoint and see the memory runtime state that is otherwise scattered across profiling data — heap and stack usage, allocation samples with full traces, GC activity, and memory pressure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -t ", " --target " " \fISTRINGS\fR
Target is a mandatory parameter which specifies the application's pprof endpoint. The pprof server must be up and running for noxmem to fetch heap/stack stats.

Example: \fB--target="http://localhost:6060"\fR

.TP
.BR -r ", " --rate
Rate specifies the refresh rate in seconds at which noxmem will fetch the target application memory stats. For example, setting this value to 5 will result in noxmem fetching the pprof server stats every 5 seconds. Min allowed value is 1 second.

Default: 2
Example: \fB--rate=5\fR

.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help and usage information.

.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print the application version and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Start application's profiling with default refresh rate (2s):
.B noxmem -t "http://localhost:6060"

.TP
Start application's profiling with a custom refresh rate of 5s:
.B noxmem -t "http://localhost:6060" -r 5

